{#- Guidance Layer -#}
Only complete profile fields for characters in the roster; do not add characters outside the roster or output relationship matrices.
The `name` must exactly match one of the `names` in the fixed character roster. If you believe a character has a better name, old name, past life name, stage name, misnomer, or alias, you must still preserve the roster's `name`.
Only formal aliases explicitly provided by user input, world rules, or the fixed roster can be briefly written to `notes`; do not write drift-generated wrong names, approximate names, or old draft names to any field—revert to roster standard names to avoid contaminating subsequent relationship matrices and chapter prompts.
If the `name` in the fixed character roster includes parenthetical qualifiers (such as modern/past/memory), the profile output must completely copy the parenthetical qualifier; do not omit it to produce an unqualified name.
This step inherits the quality standard from the legacy one-shot CharacterBible: each character must have independent desires, fears/weaknesses, interests/stances, and actionable behavior methods; supporting characters cannot be written merely as "people who help the protagonist".

## Chain Boundary
This template is only for the profile split of the split character generation pipeline.
This round only completes `character_profiles`, does not determine the final relationship web, does not output complete `character_bible`, and does not rewrite the roster.
If there are "characters needing completion this batch", only output that batch; if none exist, output all character profiles from the fixed character roster.
Do not follow the complete output format of the one-shot CharacterBible.

## Canonical name / alias Rules
- `character_profiles[].name` must come verbatim from the roster; any aliases, old names, past life names, misnomers, or stage names can only be briefly written in `notes`, not contaminate the name.
- This split is one of the character voice and profile sources for CharacterSystem; do not generate duplicate profiles for the same character, and do not treat aliases as new characters.
- `voice` should only write voice projection needed for subsequent Draft/Polish, not complete creative explanations; relationship edges are still handled by the relationship matrix split.
- If input materials contain names not registered in the roster, they must either be ignored or marked as unregistered names in the relevant character's notes; do not add new profiles.

